### Talita Cumi API. Run with the IntelliJ HTTP client or VS Code REST Client.
### Start the API with ADMIN_TOKEN=dev-admin for the admin requests.
@api = http://localhost:8080
@admin = dev-admin

### 1. A therapist signs up (hidden from search until verified)
POST {{api}}/api/therapists
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "account": { "name": "Marta Oliveira", "email": "marta@example.com", "phone": "(11) 98765-4321", "password": "segredo123" },
  "crp": "06/123456",
  "profile": {
    "approach": "Terapia Cognitivo-Comportamental",
    "bio": "Acolho mulheres em momentos de ansiedade, luto e recomeço.",
    "faithNote": "Integro a fé cristã quando a cliente deseja, sempre respeitando seu tempo.",
    "topics": ["ANXIETY", "GRIEF", "FAITH_CRISIS"],
    "city": "São Paulo",
    "modality": "BOTH",
    "sessionMinutes": 50,
    "priceCents": 15000
  }
}

### 2. Who is waiting for verification
GET {{api}}/api/admin/therapists/pending
X-Admin-Token: {{admin}}

### 3. Publish her profile (paste the id from step 1 or 2)
@therapistId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{api}}/api/admin/therapists/{{therapistId}}/verify
X-Admin-Token: {{admin}}

### 4. Search
GET {{api}}/api/therapists?topic=ANXIETY&modality=ONLINE

### 5. Free times on a day (after she sets her hours in /painel)
GET {{api}}/api/therapists/{{therapistId}}/slots?date=2026-11-02

### 6. A client signs up (the response sets the session cookie used by the next request)
POST {{api}}/api/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ana", "email": "ana@example.com", "phone": "(21) 99876-5432", "password": "segredo123" }

### 7. Book (startsAt from step 5)
POST {{api}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "therapistId": "{{therapistId}}", "startsAt": "2026-11-02T12:00:00Z", "note": "Tenho tido crises de ansiedade.", "wantsFaith": true }

### 8. My sessions
GET {{api}}/api/appointments/me
